Subject: [PATCH] mega_moe: single-kernel small-M path for DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (5120 / 2304)

- small_m_eligible: admit model_dim 5120 / inter_dim 2304 besides 7168 / 3072.
- small_m_config: buckets <= 8 pick tile_n 256, which gives V4.1 18 GEMM1 n-tiles; the XCD split needs
  a multiple of 4, so fall back to tile_n 128 (36 n-tiles, as every larger bucket uses).
Base: amd-aiter 0.1.29 as shipped in vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:nightly 54bc7a906a24.
---
diff --git a/aiter/ops/flydsl/kernels/mega_moe/mega_moe_v2.py b/aiter/ops/flydsl/kernels/mega_moe/mega_moe_v2.py
--- a/aiter/ops/flydsl/kernels/mega_moe/mega_moe_v2.py
+++ b/aiter/ops/flydsl/kernels/mega_moe/mega_moe_v2.py
@@ -91,18 +91,19 @@
     fanout_masks: tuple[int, ...] = (),
     act: str = "silu",
 ) -> bool:
-    """Whether the small-input path supports this layout (EP8 DeepSeek-V4 a8w4).
+    """Whether the small-input path supports this layout (EP8 DeepSeek-V4 / V4.1-Flash a8w4).
 
     The kernel splits its work across 8 XCDs by XCC id, so it needs the 8-XCD
     (256-CU) gfx950 parts; a 4-XCD part would leave half the work unclaimed.
+    V4.1-Flash (5120 / 2304) uses the default small-input config unchanged; it
+    was checked against an FP32 reference and against the main path on 8x MI355X.
     """
     return (
         enabled
         and arch.split(":", 1)[0] == "gfx950"
         and num_cu == 256
         and world_size == 8
-        and model_dim == 7168
-        and inter_dim == 3072
+        and (model_dim, inter_dim) in ((7168, 3072), (5120, 2304))
         and experts == 384
         and topk == 6
         and quant == "a8w4"
diff --git a/aiter/ops/flydsl/kernels/mega_moe/mega_moe_small_m.py b/aiter/ops/flydsl/kernels/mega_moe/mega_moe_small_m.py
--- a/aiter/ops/flydsl/kernels/mega_moe/mega_moe_small_m.py
+++ b/aiter/ops/flydsl/kernels/mega_moe/mega_moe_small_m.py
@@ -1447,6 +1447,10 @@
             stage1=replace(config.stage1, sort_block_m=64),
             stage2=replace(config.stage2, block_m=64),
         )
+    if (2 * inter_dim // config.stage1.tile_n) % 4:
+        # The XCD split needs whole groups of 4 GEMM1 n-tiles. The tile_n 256 of buckets <= 8 gives
+        # V4.1-Flash (inter_dim 2304) 18 n-tiles; 128 gives 36, as every larger bucket uses.
+        config = replace(config, stage1=replace(config.stage1, tile_n=128))
     return config
 
 
